    "body": "Merchants Fleet has expanded FleetShare , its managed vehicle access program, to Puerto Rico, the company said on Oct. 20 . The operation went live Sept. 14 with 113 Merchants-managed vehicles supporting an unnamed global e-commerce company’s last-mile delivery operations on the island.\nIt is FleetShare’s first deployment outside the continental United States. Drivers at the site reserve and access vehicles through a mobile app, according to the release.\nFleetShare now covers more than 8,000 managed vehicles across North America. Merchants, which leases vehicles to package delivery companies , runs the program for last-mile delivery, utility, and other fleets that share vehicles among drivers.\n“Our expansion into Puerto Rico is more than geographic growth,” said Whitney Reynolds, vice president of FleetShare at Merchants Fleet. “It demonstrates FleetShare’s flexibility and reinforces our vision of helping organizations rethink how they manage fleet operations.”\nHow drivers get vehicles under FleetShare\nFleetShare is designed to get a driver into a vehicle without a manual key handoff, whiteboard, spreadsheet, or phone call, the release said. It pairs connected key boxes with driver profiles and reservation and assignment tools. Fleet managers track assignments, availability, and utilization in one place.\nThe key boxes run on cellular service and can be installed wherever there is power and a connection, according to Merchants’ product page . The release said the system operates independently of a customer’s Wi-Fi or local network.\nIn October 2025, Merchants added three features to FleetShare, Work Truck reported : keyless access through automaker and third-party integrations, geofencing, and end-of-use driver surveys.\nCustomer and contract terms not disclosed\nBut the release does not name the customer or disclose contract terms or pricing. Nor does it say what types of vehicles make up the Puerto Rico fleet, how they are serviced on the island, or whether more will be added.\nFor now, the 113 vehicles are the only measure of the deal’s size. Reynolds said the program is built for fleets of any size.\n“Whether a customer is operating dozens of vehicles or thousands across multiple locations, FleetShare helps simplify fleet management,” she said.\nWhy it matters: FleetShare’s Puerto Rico launch puts app-based vehicle access into a 113-vehicle last-mile operation, the program’s first outside the continental U.S. The customer, contract terms, and how the island fleet is serviced remain undisclosed.\nUpcoming FreightWaves Events\nFreightTech\nF3: Future of Freight Festival\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nOctober 27, 2026 – October 28, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nFreightTech F3: Future of Freight Festival Oct 27 – Oct 28 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now",
